<title>UK: HORSE RACING-TRAINER CRUMP DIES.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-TRAINER CRUMP DIES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Neville Crump, who trained three Grand National winners, has died at the age of 86.</p>
<p>Crump, who died on Saturday night, was Champion National Hunt trainer in 1951-52 and 1956-57 and trained Sheila's Cottage (1948), Teal (1952) and Merryman II (1960) to victory in the Grand National.</p>
</text>
